WEBVTT

00:00:01.070 --> 00:00:04.150
When were the Taika Reforms?

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:07.570
We're in third grade; you should know already! You're so dumb.

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:09.650
We haven't learned it yet.

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:11.530
It's easy to remember.

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:13.650
Call them the "uneventful reforms".

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:15.320
Uneventful?

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:18.660
Yeah, see, nothing much happened during them.

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:21.830
Uneventful six-two-five.

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:24.580
Uneventful... six-two-five.

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:26.220
Don't forget.

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:27.880
I've got it stuck in my head now,

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:30.050
so don't worry.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:40.810
Something that grows when its alone, What is it?

00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:42.090
One more chance, One more chance!

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:43.470
Never, Never give up!

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:44.770
One more chance, One more chance!

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:46.070
Never give up!

00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:59.200
Meeting with someone else is easy

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.970
I decided what to say before they even asked

00:01:01.970 --> 00:01:04.580
My heart beats fast thinking if I passed or not

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:06.760
I can't panic in this fight for love

00:01:07.190 --> 00:01:09.830
Study! Study! Study! Keeps me up all night

00:01:09.830 --> 00:01:12.460
I've got a dreaming genius inside me

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:15.040
I'd be great if everyone's wishes came true

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:17.210
I won't care about other people's lives

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:20.170
Perfect-area complete!

00:01:20.170 --> 00:01:22.800
I'll definitely be waiting for you!

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:29.200
I can hear your voice from the Perfect-area!

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:30.510
Ah! Ear! Ear!

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:33.780
Why? Why can't stop when I pass you

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:36.390
if I'm your counselor

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:38.980
"Are we friends?" Yes, we're friends."

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:40.980
But, I failed the test with a 0

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:44.290
No! I'll take it again! and again!

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:46.430
I'm serious. One more chance, please

00:01:46.430 --> 00:01:50.900
There's something better for is in the future

00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:56.990
Better than my life right now.

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:02.620
Here at Fumizuki Academy, knowledge is power...

00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:04.730
Second Period
Lilies and Roses and Health

00:02:04.730 --> 00:02:07.240
...and your test score is justice.

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:08.900
What's up, Himeji?

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:09.910
Got something for me?

00:02:09.910 --> 00:02:13.890
Well, I wanted to ask you about something...

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:15.090
May I have a moment?

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:27.430
Class F ended up winning the first sophomore ESB.

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:30.390
They're better than I thought.

00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:34.940
The class that lost to them must be angry about having their facilities downgraded.

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:40.890
Well, maybe that'll teach them that they
need to study hard in order to win battles.

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:42.410
Life itself is a battle, after a-

00:02:42.410 --> 00:02:44.550
Actually...

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:48.240
The students personally requested that they not swap facilities.

00:02:49.070 --> 00:02:50.560
What?

00:02:56.430 --> 00:02:58.640
It ain't called superglue for nothing.

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:00.670
They're as good as new in no time flat.

00:03:00.670 --> 00:03:04.260
We should feel blessed that we're afforded the luxury of such high quality glue.

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:09.560
It's only natural to upgrade your
supplies after winning a tough battle.

00:03:11.010 --> 00:03:14.600
Man, but we could be using class E's desks right now...

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:18.270
Yuuji, why the hell did you turn down the trade?

00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:19.670
Seriously, man?

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:22.110
You like those shitty desks?

00:03:22.110 --> 00:03:26.070
They're better than these damn flimsy tables!

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:37.920
You don't study anyway, so what difference does it make to you?

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:39.640
A big one!

00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:42.340
I eat on it, I sleep on it, and I draw on it.

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:43.190
<b>Akihisa
Mizuki.</b>

00:03:43.190 --> 00:03:43.600
I eat on it, I sleep on it, and I draw on it.

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:46.930
As you can see, my desk is an important part of my school experience!

00:03:46.930 --> 00:03:49.350
They share the same heart.

00:03:49.350 --> 00:03:51.980
This is the last day we'll be using them.

00:03:51.980 --> 00:03:55.310
Class A declared war on us, yeah?

00:03:56.430 --> 00:03:59.800
We're gonna beat them and start using their facilities.

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:02.320
The situation's not exactly what I had in mind, but we should do just fine.

00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:06.210
My predictions allowed for a certain margin of error.

00:04:06.210 --> 00:04:07.280
Right, Himeji?

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:10.330
Yes...

00:04:12.220 --> 00:04:15.040
Come on, let's go to class A.

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:18.830
So this is class A.

00:04:18.830 --> 00:04:21.350
It looks more like a five star hotel.

00:04:22.070 --> 00:04:26.290
This is how I should be spending my school days!

00:04:26.290 --> 00:04:30.350
Oh my god, Yoshii! They have a self-serving bar with snacks!

00:04:31.150 --> 00:04:34.310
You're gonna get taken advantage of if that's all it takes to impress you.

00:04:34.310 --> 00:04:36.570
Man up.

00:04:36.570 --> 00:04:39.730
Practice what you preach.

00:04:39.730 --> 00:04:42.570
Oh? Isn't the ESB tomorrow?

00:04:42.810 --> 00:04:43.940
Sister!

00:04:43.940 --> 00:04:45.750
Surrendering already?

00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:49.100
We're just here to check out our new facilities.

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:51.160
Ohh, so tough.

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:52.700
I'm here to negotiate.

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:56.210
I want a one-on-one battle
between the two class reps.

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:59.130
Are you an idiot?

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:02.040
What makes you think you can handle our class valedictorian?

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:03.380
Are you scared?

00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:08.220
I can't help but think that you're trying to take us
out while we're still recovering from the last ESB.

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:10.930
Want to go now?

00:05:10.930 --> 00:05:11.990
Hang on.

00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:17.430
I'm fine with one-on-one.

00:05:17.430 --> 00:05:18.560
Rep!

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:21.190
But I have a condition.

00:05:25.650 --> 00:05:30.110
The loser must promise to comply with an order from the winner.

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:33.870
So that was why you declared war on us?

00:05:33.870 --> 00:05:35.810
Don't jump to conclusions.

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:40.740
We have an obligation to protect the
public order and dignity of our school.

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:46.670
We must punish lazy idiots who
declare war without doing anything.

00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:51.590
Fine. The loser of the one-on-one will do whatever the winner says.

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:54.560
No, it'll be five-on-five.

00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:56.930
Yuuko.

00:05:57.320 --> 00:06:00.190
I'm not saying that I think our rep is going to lose.

00:06:00.190 --> 00:06:02.100
We just need to take some precautions, is all.

00:06:02.100 --> 00:06:05.030
Sure. Five-on-five it is.

00:06:05.030 --> 00:06:08.110
In exchange, however, we'll pick the subjects.

00:06:08.610 --> 00:06:09.660
Very well.

00:06:11.390 --> 00:06:12.950
Negotiation complete.

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:16.410
What now, Yuuji?

00:06:16.410 --> 00:06:18.800
Don't worry. We're still gonna win.

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:21.840
All that's changed is that we get the honor of bossing them around.

00:06:22.530 --> 00:06:24.380
Are you sure we should go through with this.

00:06:24.380 --> 00:06:28.370
I've heard some nasty rumors about Shouko Kirishima, class A's rep.

00:06:28.370 --> 00:06:28.920
Rumors?

00:06:29.270 --> 00:06:31.960
She's smart and she's not half-bad looking either.

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:35.640
But she doesn't have a boyfriend or
anything. Never even hangs out with guys.

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:38.350
Yeah, she does seem like the popular type.

00:06:38.610 --> 00:06:41.270
So, the rumors say she has no interest in guys.

00:06:41.550 --> 00:06:43.750
No interest in-?

00:06:44.690 --> 00:06:47.610
Holy shit, so her goal is...!?

00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:54.430
No frickin' way.

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:58.690
There's no way that could be
happening right under our noses.

00:06:58.690 --> 00:06:59.790
Right, Shimada?

00:07:00.360 --> 00:07:04.520
No, I'm sure it could be happening.

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:06.670
I found you, mistress!

00:07:07.180 --> 00:07:08.100
Miharu!?

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:09.650
You're so mean!

00:07:09.650 --> 00:07:13.810
How could you drink tea with these disgusting faggots instead of hanging out with me?

00:07:13.810 --> 00:07:15.740
Let go! Get the hell offa me!

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:16.580
Mistress!

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:17.390
Who the hell is that?
Mistress!

00:07:17.770 --> 00:07:20.740
Miharu Shimizu of class 2D.

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:22.760
Stop it! Get the hell away from me!

00:07:22.760 --> 00:07:25.470
Don't be so shy, mistress.

00:07:25.470 --> 00:07:29.740
I know you love me - you don't need to hide it!

00:07:29.740 --> 00:07:32.750
I'm not a dyke!

00:07:32.750 --> 00:07:34.660
Help me out here, Yoshii!

00:07:34.660 --> 00:07:38.580
She's right, Shimizu. Being gay is wrong.

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:43.680
While it's true that Shimada looks like a guy, acts like a guy, and has the chest of a guy...

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:46.140
...she's a pro wrestler in disguise!

00:07:46.990 --> 00:07:49.000
I'm totally feminine in all areas!

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:53.420
Exactly! I love my mistress's feminine traits!

00:07:54.800 --> 00:07:57.250
A-almost...

00:07:57.250 --> 00:08:00.510
Shimada, stop! I'll do whatever you say!

00:08:01.100 --> 00:08:02.360
Seriously?

00:08:02.360 --> 00:08:06.060
Then I want you to treat me to
crepes at Lapelle's next weekend.

00:08:06.760 --> 00:08:08.880
I'm kinda low on cash-

00:08:09.680 --> 00:08:11.780
Fine, I'll treat you!

00:08:11.780 --> 00:08:15.130
Also, you have to call me "honey" from now on.

00:08:15.130 --> 00:08:16.410
And I'll call you Aki.

00:08:17.030 --> 00:08:18.700
Yes, honey!

00:08:18.700 --> 00:08:20.920
And... And...

00:08:22.590 --> 00:08:25.910
S-say you love me!

00:08:25.910 --> 00:08:27.460
S-s...

00:08:27.460 --> 00:08:29.250
You won't do it.

00:08:29.250 --> 00:08:30.890
Say it!

00:08:31.670 --> 00:08:34.220
A-almost...

00:08:34.220 --> 00:08:37.220
Hurry up and say you love me.

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:39.040
Okay!

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:41.310
"Hurry up and say you love me"!

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:45.890
You dumbass!

00:08:45.890 --> 00:08:47.810
N-n-no! You're gonna break it!
You dumbass!

00:08:50.780 --> 00:08:52.980
Man, I thought I was toast.

00:08:53.460 --> 00:08:54.440
Himeji?

00:08:56.080 --> 00:08:58.070
What're you doing, Himeji?

00:08:58.740 --> 00:08:59.570
Yoshii!?

00:09:09.420 --> 00:09:12.250
This looks like a love letter.

00:09:12.800 --> 00:09:12.960
But who would write a love letter in the classroom?

00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:14.340
Get a clue. What else would it be?

00:09:14.340 --> 00:09:16.510
that I'm in love with you.
I finally realized
Get a clue. What else would it be?

00:09:16.510 --> 00:09:16.900
Get a clue. What else would it be?

00:09:16.900 --> 00:09:17.670
Umm... I think you have the wrong idea about this...

00:09:17.670 --> 00:09:19.880
The proof is right in your hands.

00:09:19.880 --> 00:09:22.230
Actually, maybe not...

00:09:22.230 --> 00:09:22.550
But no, it is!

00:09:22.550 --> 00:09:22.970
Come on, just admit it.
But no, it is!

00:09:22.970 --> 00:09:23.460
...love you.

00:09:23.460 --> 00:09:25.830
Come on, just admit it.

00:09:25.830 --> 00:09:28.180
What a depressing chain letter...

00:09:28.180 --> 00:09:28.240
God dammit, just deal with it!

00:09:28.240 --> 00:09:31.330
Things will get weird if you misunderstand.

00:09:31.330 --> 00:09:31.690
Is he in our class?

00:09:31.690 --> 00:09:33.150
Yuuji is in our class, obviously.

00:09:33.150 --> 00:09:33.900
Yes.

00:09:33.900 --> 00:09:34.440
I see.

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:35.070
There's no point in forcing yourself.

00:09:35.070 --> 00:09:38.900
Hey, I'll teach you how to write depressing chain mail properly.

00:09:38.900 --> 00:09:39.030
There's no point in forcing yourself.

00:09:39.190 --> 00:09:39.700
No, this isn't a chain letter!

00:09:39.700 --> 00:09:42.410
Do you even know how!?

00:09:42.410 --> 00:09:44.410
But it is!
Do you even know how!?

00:09:44.410 --> 00:09:44.550
Do you even know how!?

00:09:44.550 --> 00:09:46.950
Because the world is crashing down around me.

00:09:46.950 --> 00:09:49.090
Have some tea and calm down.

00:09:49.090 --> 00:09:50.160
No, it's not.

00:09:50.160 --> 00:09:50.360
Have some tea and calm down.

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:52.800
Seriously? What do you see in him?

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:54.380
He's not even good-looking.

00:09:54.380 --> 00:09:55.290
No, it's not about his looks...

00:09:55.290 --> 00:09:56.980
Look in the mirror.

00:09:56.980 --> 00:09:58.620
I mean, I like how he looks!

00:09:58.620 --> 00:10:04.200
My friend told me that when two handsome guys like you and Sakamoto walk together,

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:05.650
it's like a painting.

00:10:05.650 --> 00:10:08.790
She sounds like a great friend. Treat her well.

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:10.060
She also told me that you're the bottom in the relationship.

00:10:10.060 --> 00:10:11.180
Yuuji is definitely a better fit for Himeji.

00:10:11.180 --> 00:10:11.270
She also told me that you're the bottom in the relationship.

00:10:11.270 --> 00:10:11.390
I don't think you should be friends with her.

00:10:11.390 --> 00:10:13.180
Maybe I still have a chance.

00:10:13.180 --> 00:10:16.820
But he's also beautiful on the inside!

00:10:16.820 --> 00:10:19.120
Yeah, his liver is pretty solid.

00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:21.070
I'm not talking about his organs!

00:10:21.070 --> 00:10:21.280
Are you really that far in denial?

00:10:21.280 --> 00:10:22.860
You can't be telling me that you like his personality.

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:27.510
I am. He's so kind and cheerful.
There's always a smile on his face.

00:10:27.510 --> 00:10:29.950
I've always admired him.

00:10:30.350 --> 00:10:32.920
I see... Well...

00:10:32.920 --> 00:10:34.210
Yes?

00:10:34.830 --> 00:10:36.920
I hope you hear the reply you wanted to.

00:10:37.620 --> 00:10:38.470
Thank you.

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:41.870
There you are.

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:43.590
We're about to begin our strategy meeting.

00:10:45.590 --> 00:10:48.060
Hey, where are you going? Akihisa!

00:10:48.060 --> 00:10:49.670
Stay away from me.

00:10:49.670 --> 00:10:50.930
Don't walk with me.

00:10:51.200 --> 00:10:53.850
What's wrong? Did something happen?

00:10:53.850 --> 00:10:55.980
I... I...

00:10:57.150 --> 00:10:59.320
I'm not the bottom!

00:11:00.040 --> 00:11:01.110
What?

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:06.580
Elites vs. Idiots
All right, let's begin round one.

00:11:06.580 --> 00:11:08.680
Why am I the round girl?
Elites vs. Idiots

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:09.410
Round one.

00:11:09.410 --> 00:11:10.670
What are you talking about?

00:11:10.670 --> 00:11:13.310
There's no one more suited for it than you.

00:11:13.310 --> 00:11:15.690
But I'm not a girl.

00:11:15.990 --> 00:11:18.280
Would both contestants please step forward?

00:11:20.230 --> 00:11:21.700
Good luck, Shimada.

00:11:21.970 --> 00:11:23.820
Off I go.

00:11:24.150 --> 00:11:28.620
Let's make this quick. I don't feel like prolonging a battle with someone who's going to lose anyway.

00:11:28.620 --> 00:11:31.000
You're in for a shock if you think I'm weak just 'cause I'm in class F.

00:11:32.100 --> 00:11:33.540
Begin!

00:11:36.210 --> 00:11:37.910
Summoning Being!

00:11:37.910 --> 00:11:38.820
Summon!

00:11:40.790 --> 00:11:45.310
My math is at class B level.

00:11:45.310 --> 00:11:47.690
Wow, cool.

00:11:47.690 --> 00:11:48.680
Summon!

00:11:54.060 --> 00:11:55.450
N-no way...

00:11:55.450 --> 00:11:58.280
I'm in class A, you know.

00:11:58.580 --> 00:12:01.150
Victor: Yuuko Kinoshita of class A.

00:12:03.730 --> 00:12:05.090
Not an unexpected turn of events.

00:12:05.090 --> 00:12:09.920
I mean, you forgot that class A is higher than class B-

00:12:09.920 --> 00:12:10.450
A-almost...

00:12:10.450 --> 00:12:13.370
I'm kind of enjoying this.

00:12:13.370 --> 00:12:14.630
Round two.

00:12:14.630 --> 00:12:16.340
Let's commence with round two.

00:12:16.340 --> 00:12:17.540
Would both contestants please step forward?

00:12:18.620 --> 00:12:20.950
I'm class A's Miho Satou.

00:12:23.420 --> 00:12:25.970
It's all you, Akihisa.

00:12:25.970 --> 00:12:28.370
Me? We're screwed if we lose this one.

00:12:28.370 --> 00:12:30.810
Don't give me that. I believe in you.

00:12:31.090 --> 00:12:34.350
So you want me to get serious?

00:12:34.350 --> 00:12:35.420
Yeah.

00:12:35.420 --> 00:12:37.240
You can stop hiding it now.

00:12:37.240 --> 00:12:39.690
Show everyone your true strength.

00:12:39.690 --> 00:12:41.900
Man, you don't make it easy for me.

00:12:41.900 --> 00:12:43.960
Don't tell me you're...

00:12:43.960 --> 00:12:47.570
Yeah. You'll be the first to see my true power.

00:12:47.570 --> 00:12:49.490
So you really are...

00:12:49.490 --> 00:12:50.590
Correct.

00:12:50.590 --> 00:12:55.090
I've always kept it a secret, but I'm actually...

00:12:55.740 --> 00:12:57.240
left-handed.

00:13:00.680 --> 00:13:03.470
Victor: Miho Satou of class A.

00:13:03.470 --> 00:13:07.560
What the hell does being left-handed have to do with your test scores!?

00:13:07.560 --> 00:13:09.720
A-almost...

00:13:09.720 --> 00:13:11.700
Now's when it really starts.

00:13:11.700 --> 00:13:12.390
Time to get serious.

00:13:12.710 --> 00:13:15.850
You bastard! I thought you said you believed in me!

00:13:15.850 --> 00:13:18.520
I believed that you'd lose!

00:13:18.520 --> 00:13:21.690
I'm gonna punch you in the balls with my left hand!

00:13:22.860 --> 00:13:24.540
Round three will now begin.
Round three.

00:13:24.540 --> 00:13:25.290
Round three will now begin.

00:13:25.490 --> 00:13:27.420
Class A: Aiko Kudou.

00:13:27.420 --> 00:13:29.030
Class F: Kouta Tsuchiya.

00:13:30.870 --> 00:13:32.240
What subject?

00:13:32.580 --> 00:13:33.910
Health.

00:13:33.910 --> 00:13:37.780
I hear you're pretty good with health.

00:13:37.780 --> 00:13:42.090
But I'm pretty good at it too - in a different way.

00:13:42.360 --> 00:13:43.300
I use the knowledge <i>practically</i>.

00:13:43.300 --> 00:13:44.830
Practically?

00:13:48.340 --> 00:13:49.890
Voyeur!

00:13:49.890 --> 00:13:50.530
Carnivore vs. Voyeur

00:13:50.530 --> 00:13:53.560
How dare you do that to Voyeur!

00:13:53.560 --> 00:13:54.310
Cheapskate!

00:13:54.570 --> 00:13:56.720
You're going to sub for him?

00:13:56.720 --> 00:13:59.060
Anyone can tell that you're hopeless, though.

00:13:59.060 --> 00:14:02.660
I can teach you health if you want.

00:14:02.660 --> 00:14:05.310
<i>Practically</i>, of course.

00:14:06.110 --> 00:14:07.320
Yoshii!

00:14:07.320 --> 00:14:07.780
Aki!

00:14:08.370 --> 00:14:11.840
Mind your own business! He's never gonna get the chance to do it!

00:14:11.840 --> 00:14:15.160
Exactly! He doesn't need the knowledge!

00:14:15.160 --> 00:14:18.140
Why are you saying that!?

00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:20.000
Voyeur!

00:14:20.810 --> 00:14:22.920
This is nothing.

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:25.210
All right, let the battle commence.

00:14:25.730 --> 00:14:27.000
Summon.

00:14:27.000 --> 00:14:28.100
Summon!

00:14:32.050 --> 00:14:33.430
Over 400?

00:14:33.430 --> 00:14:37.550
Practical vs. theoretical. I'll show you which is stronger.

00:14:40.060 --> 00:14:42.340
See ya, Mr. Voyeur.

00:14:42.340 --> 00:14:43.190
Acceleration...

00:14:45.590 --> 00:14:47.180
...complete.

00:14:49.070 --> 00:14:51.200
I-I lost?

00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:54.110
Victor: Kouta Tsuchiya of class F.

00:14:54.110 --> 00:14:58.160
Wow! His health score is on par with my comprehensive score!

00:14:58.160 --> 00:14:59.840
Round four.

00:14:59.840 --> 00:15:00.500
All right, let's begin round four.

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:02.550
Wish me luck.

00:15:02.550 --> 00:15:04.090
Good luck, Himeji!

00:15:04.090 --> 00:15:04.840
Thanks.

00:15:05.080 --> 00:15:07.010
I'll be her opponent.

00:15:08.420 --> 00:15:10.360
Toshimitsu Kubo, huh?

00:15:10.360 --> 00:15:11.960
This is the key round.

00:15:11.960 --> 00:15:13.020
Why?

00:15:13.020 --> 00:15:14.770
He's #2 in our year.

00:15:14.770 --> 00:15:17.170
This is gonna be tough if we don't pick something he's bad at.

00:15:17.170 --> 00:15:17.970
No way...

00:15:18.290 --> 00:15:20.570
So, what subject?

00:15:20.570 --> 00:15:22.700
Comprehensive.

00:15:22.700 --> 00:15:25.210
Wait, we have the right to decide-

00:15:25.210 --> 00:15:26.000
Don't worry.

00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:26.980
Himeji?

00:15:27.220 --> 00:15:28.410
Crap...

00:15:28.410 --> 00:15:31.710
Comprehensive basically means that your class rank translates directly into your strength.

00:15:31.710 --> 00:15:32.410
That means...

00:15:34.410 --> 00:15:36.280
Start battle.

00:15:36.760 --> 00:15:37.490
Summon.

00:15:43.420 --> 00:15:45.150
Look at those points.

00:15:45.150 --> 00:15:48.050
That's how strong #2 is?

00:15:48.050 --> 00:15:48.710
Himeji!

00:15:49.060 --> 00:15:50.910
Summoning Being...

00:15:52.140 --> 00:15:53.020
Summon!

00:15:55.090 --> 00:15:56.920
Over 4000?

00:15:56.920 --> 00:15:59.430
Her points are on par with the valedictorian.

00:15:59.430 --> 00:16:01.920
When the hell did you...

00:16:01.920 --> 00:16:02.600
Go!

00:16:02.950 --> 00:16:05.480
I decided to give it my best shot.

00:16:07.870 --> 00:16:11.740
I had been wondering why we
even had ESBs in the first place.

00:16:12.070 --> 00:16:13.150
Imagination

00:16:13.150 --> 00:16:16.050
I like this class...

00:16:16.050 --> 00:16:16.650
Imagination

00:16:16.650 --> 00:16:21.290
because everyone helps each other out with all they have...

00:16:21.290 --> 00:16:22.130
Imagination

00:16:22.130 --> 00:16:25.230
because the person I like is in this class.

00:16:25.230 --> 00:16:25.860
Imagination

00:16:25.860 --> 00:16:28.690
So I won't let you guys down!

00:16:28.690 --> 00:16:32.670
Imagination

00:16:36.200 --> 00:16:38.850
Victor: Mizuki Himeji of class F.

00:16:38.850 --> 00:16:40.630
Hear that, Aki?

00:16:40.630 --> 00:16:42.480
It's an even split now!

00:16:43.240 --> 00:16:43.890
Himeji...

00:16:43.890 --> 00:16:47.050
The next match will determine everything.

00:16:48.820 --> 00:16:49.180
Round five.

00:16:49.180 --> 00:16:52.240
All right, let's begin the last round.

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:54.610
It's finally my turn.

00:16:54.610 --> 00:16:55.450
Yuuji...

00:16:55.450 --> 00:16:56.410
Watch and learn.

00:16:56.730 --> 00:16:59.600
I'm class F's rep, Yuuji Sakamoto.

00:16:59.600 --> 00:17:03.270
I'm class A's rep, Shouko Kirishima.

00:17:03.270 --> 00:17:04.830
What subject?

00:17:05.110 --> 00:17:08.840
I choose a restricted Japanese
history test for the final round.

00:17:08.840 --> 00:17:13.050
The material will be of the elementary school level. The maximum points will be 100.

00:17:13.050 --> 00:17:14.530
A testing showdown!?

00:17:14.530 --> 00:17:16.380
Not a Being battle?

00:17:16.380 --> 00:17:21.350
What's a test showdown?
The ESB is a battle utilizing your test scores.

00:17:21.350 --> 00:17:21.580
The ESB is a battle utilizing your test scores.

00:17:21.580 --> 00:17:24.890
As long as it involves tests in some ways and is approved by a teacher,

00:17:24.890 --> 00:17:26.810
it doesn't matter how you go about it.

00:17:27.060 --> 00:17:29.830
Very well. Prepare yourselves.

00:17:29.830 --> 00:17:32.230
Both contestants, please head to the classroom.

00:17:34.450 --> 00:17:36.250
Have you lost your mind, Yuuji?

00:17:36.250 --> 00:17:40.840
Won't both of you get 100s if it's at an elementary school level?

00:17:40.840 --> 00:17:42.760
Isn't it just going to end in a draw?

00:17:42.760 --> 00:17:46.370
No. A simple mistake means you lose it all.

00:17:47.520 --> 00:17:48.890
Exactly.

00:17:48.890 --> 00:17:52.540
This is a test of endurance and concentration, not academics.

00:17:52.540 --> 00:17:53.080
Yuuji...

00:17:53.080 --> 00:17:55.550
Don't sweat it. I have this in the bag.

00:17:55.550 --> 00:17:58.920
Once Shouko memorizes
something, she'll never forget it.

00:17:58.920 --> 00:18:01.760
Doesn't that mean you're at a disadvantage, then? You're dealing with history.

00:18:01.760 --> 00:18:04.370
No, that's the point.

00:18:04.370 --> 00:18:11.480
She memorized the Taika Reforms as taking place in the year 625.

00:18:12.520 --> 00:18:15.940
If that question appears on the test, victory is mine.

00:18:15.940 --> 00:18:17.310
Wait, Yuuji.

00:18:18.690 --> 00:18:22.120
I thought the Taika Reforms <i>did</i> take place in the year 625.

00:18:22.120 --> 00:18:24.740
No, they took place in 645.

00:18:25.380 --> 00:18:26.960
I'm positive.

00:18:26.960 --> 00:18:28.490
Trust me, Akihisa.

00:18:28.490 --> 00:18:29.290
Yuuji...

00:18:29.290 --> 00:18:33.710
Those system desks are ours.

00:18:39.030 --> 00:18:41.180
Please begin.

00:18:42.930 --> 00:18:44.310
It started.

00:18:44.980 --> 00:18:48.000
What happens if that question doesn't appear?

00:18:48.000 --> 00:18:51.610
Well, if his endurance and concentration aren't as good as hers, then we'll lose.

00:18:51.610 --> 00:18:53.320
But if it does appear...

00:18:53.320 --> 00:18:54.650
Please answer the following questions:

00:18:54.650 --> 00:18:58.660
Who did Oda Nobunaga make an alliance with in the Battle of Nagashino?

00:18:58.660 --> 00:19:03.700
Who signed the Harris Treaty with American Consul General Harris?

00:19:03.700 --> 00:19:05.710
When did the Taika Reforms take place?

00:19:05.710 --> 00:19:06.700
There it is!
When did the Taika Reforms take place?

00:19:06.700 --> 00:19:19.220
When did the Taika Reforms take place?

00:19:26.500 --> 00:19:29.730
I shall hereby announce the scores for the restricted exam.

00:19:29.730 --> 00:19:32.230
Class A representative, Shouko Kirishima:

00:19:33.260 --> 00:19:34.900
97 points.

00:19:35.760 --> 00:19:37.450
Yes!

00:19:37.450 --> 00:19:40.170
She didn't ace it!

00:19:40.170 --> 00:19:42.740
We're gonna live like kings!

00:19:43.040 --> 00:19:44.270
Yoshii!

00:19:44.860 --> 00:19:48.580
Next, class F's rep, Yuuji Sakamoto:

00:19:53.810 --> 00:19:55.090
53 points.

00:19:58.940 --> 00:20:02.230
Class F ended up trading their coffee tables for cardboard boxes.

00:20:07.550 --> 00:20:16.620
Baka, go go home!

00:20:16.910 --> 00:20:19.890
It's a time of peace now that school's out

00:20:19.890 --> 00:20:21.440
If I were to compare her

00:20:21.440 --> 00:20:22.980
"She's a real angel!"

00:20:22.980 --> 00:20:25.950
Then a sudden note ruined my fun

00:20:25.950 --> 00:20:27.340
It said I have a makeup test!

00:20:27.340 --> 00:20:28.730
It's hell!

00:20:29.060 --> 00:20:32.070
I was joking with my friends,

00:20:32.070 --> 00:20:35.100
"There's no way someone is that stupid!"

00:20:35.100 --> 00:20:38.180
But deep down inside,

00:20:38.180 --> 00:20:39.470
I was screaming,

00:20:39.470 --> 00:20:42.430
"That was me! I'm that stupid!"

00:20:42.850 --> 00:20:49.010
I thought the "Monthly" sign in the parking lot

00:20:49.010 --> 00:20:54.290
was the company's name!

00:20:54.290 --> 00:20:57.040
For the longest time...

00:20:57.740 --> 00:21:00.740
Stupidity is a manly character

00:21:00.740 --> 00:21:03.440
Is that our lack of common sense?

00:21:03.440 --> 00:21:06.750
Rules are useless in this world

00:21:06.750 --> 00:21:09.750
Eat Korean BBQ every night and overthrow the masses!

00:21:09.750 --> 00:21:11.390
Look!

00:21:11.390 --> 00:21:15.960
The sun that rose from the west is now setting down.

00:21:15.960 --> 00:21:19.000
Run! It's almost dinner time.

00:21:19.000 --> 00:21:25.870
Let's go home!

00:21:33.460 --> 00:21:34.850
We're even worse off than before!

00:21:35.400 --> 00:21:38.060
What the hell was with that score!?

00:21:38.060 --> 00:21:39.850
That's my ability.

00:21:39.850 --> 00:21:42.980
If you couldn't get 100, then what the hell was the point?

00:21:42.980 --> 00:21:46.050
I never thought there'd be an ambush.

00:21:46.050 --> 00:21:48.830
What ambush!?

00:21:48.830 --> 00:21:49.720
Yuuji.

00:21:50.290 --> 00:21:52.410
Our promise.

00:21:52.720 --> 00:21:55.960
We promised to comply with their order if we lost.

00:21:55.960 --> 00:21:58.080
Fine, what is it?

00:21:59.680 --> 00:22:01.280
You can't do this, Kirishima!

00:22:01.280 --> 00:22:03.210
Homosexuality is unacceptable!

00:22:05.380 --> 00:22:08.340
Yuuji, go out with me.

00:22:10.510 --> 00:22:13.080
You still haven't given up?

00:22:13.080 --> 00:22:14.890
I'll never give up.

00:22:14.890 --> 00:22:17.100
I'll always love you.

00:22:17.100 --> 00:22:18.060
Can I refuse?

00:22:18.060 --> 00:22:20.050
No, we promised.

00:22:20.050 --> 00:22:21.720
We're going on a date right now.

00:22:21.720 --> 00:22:22.470
Wai-

00:22:28.990 --> 00:22:31.030
Wait, what?

00:22:31.030 --> 00:22:32.660
Just what the hell is going on here?

00:22:32.660 --> 00:22:36.140
So Kirishima only kept staring at Himeji because...

00:22:36.140 --> 00:22:39.790
She wanted to make sure Himeji wasn't doing anything funny with Yuuji.

00:22:39.790 --> 00:22:42.670
Sorry about this, Himeji.

00:22:42.970 --> 00:22:45.470
Our classroom sucks even more than before.

00:22:45.470 --> 00:22:48.380
No, this is a fabulous room.

00:22:48.730 --> 00:22:51.600
I love class F!

00:22:52.610 --> 00:22:53.790
And...

00:22:55.770 --> 00:22:59.630
All right, Aki. You're going to treat me to some crepes.

00:22:59.630 --> 00:23:02.240
Hold on! I thought we were
gonna go on this weekend...

00:23:02.240 --> 00:23:04.720
Weekends are weekends. Today is today.

00:23:04.720 --> 00:23:06.960
That means that I have to treat you twice!

00:23:06.960 --> 00:23:09.070
I won't have any money left to feed
myself until my parents send me more!

00:23:09.260 --> 00:23:10.200
No.

00:23:10.200 --> 00:23:13.510
He's going to watch a movie with me.

00:23:14.110 --> 00:23:16.960
I don't remember agreeing to that...

00:23:16.960 --> 00:23:18.960
That's because I just decided on it.

00:23:18.960 --> 00:23:21.900
Hurry up, you're treating me to crepes!

00:23:21.900 --> 00:23:24.390
What movie are we going to watch?

00:23:24.390 --> 00:23:26.590
No!

00:23:26.590 --> 00:23:29.380
My living expenses! My nutrition! Save me!

00:23:29.380 --> 00:23:30.010
Wait, my hands are going to break!

00:23:30.010 --> 00:23:34.080
I'm starting to wonder if he's really an idiot or not.

00:23:35.980 --> 00:23:37.020
Question three:

00:23:37.020 --> 00:23:41.750
What is the ratio of one's income spent on food known as?

00:23:41.750 --> 00:23:43.410
I'm not gonna be able to afford
anything except salt and water this week.

00:23:43.410 --> 00:23:45.360
The question didn't ask you what you're going to eat.

00:23:45.360 --> 00:23:47.370
Next episode: Food Expenses and Dates and Stun Guns.

00:23:47.370 --> 00:23:49.240
This will be on your test.
